  urldate = {2024-01-25},
  abstract = {This chapter provides an assessment of socialism as an economic system in the historical context of societal development. A lot of space is devoted to the practical features of socialism, and its correspondence to the theoretical Marxist model is analysed. There is a debate whether the transformation of the capitalist economy into socialism promotes the progress of society. The similarities between serfdom and socialism characteristic of the feudal system are discussed, the reasons for this phenomenon are revealed. The conclusion is reached that in practice capitalism is a more advanced form of economic life because it is able to take into account human nature and its desires. The concept of egoism as an engine of social development, conditioning people’s motivation and opening the way to progress, is revealed. Practical examples are given to support the correctness of this conclusion.},
